 both 1946 and 1950, but in 1952 she was challenged by her teammate " [:a {:href "/athletes/77292"} "Nina Romashkova"] "."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Romashkova took the lead in the final with 50.84 (166-9¾) in the second round, and increased that with 51.42 (168-8½) in round three. That sealed the victory, as Dumbadze did not perform up to her standard, winning only a bronze medal behind fellow Soviet " [:a {:href "/athletes/77153"} "Yelizaveta Bagryantseva"] ". This was the first ever medal sweep by a nation in women’s track &amp; field athletics."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Two months after the Olympics, Dumbadze would set her final world record with 57.04 (187-1¾) at a national meeting in Tbilisi, Georgia."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Qualifying"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "486"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/77292"} "Nina Romashkova"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/URS"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/URS.png"}] "URS"]] [:td {} "45.05 (1)"] [:td {} "51.42 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "label label-default"} [:abbrev {:title "Olympic Record"} "OR"]]] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "487"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/77153"} "Yelizaveta Bagryantseva"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/URS"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/URS.png"}] "URS"]] [:td {} "40.73 (6)"] [:td {} "47.08 (2)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {:class "bib"} "485"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/77186"} "Nino Dumbadze"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/URS"} [:img {:style "padding-right